    "qp_env1": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "qp_e1_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>World-class washing technology and premium Spanish raw down are two parts of the story. The third is the Ise Plain, whose climate is ideal for refining down.</p><p>In Meiwa, Mie Prefecture, where Kawada Feather's factory is located, the groundwater is ultra-soft, with a hardness of just 3–5 mg/L. It comes from the Ōdaigahara mountains, one of the rainiest areas in Japan, and the factory uses it generously to wash down. Close to pure water, with very fine particles, ultra-soft water reaches every part of the down to remove dirt, and its strong antioxidant power helps repair damaged areas of the down.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "qp_e1_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-philosophy-ise.jpg",
        "image_link": "",
        "full_width": false,
        "image_position": "right",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "qp_env2": {
      "type": "split-content",
      "blocks": {
        "qp_e2_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Meanwhile, after the wind drops its rain over the Ōdaigahara mountains, it reaches the Ise Plain dry. Rainfall is low all year, and the air is very dry.</p><p>Down's fine branches open up as it dries, so this climate lets the factory remove even more impurities.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "qp_e2_text"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/knowledge-philosophy-testing.jpg",
